| Regional store rules (§ 13.8) | _list any per-region requirements: KSA / UAE / India / China_ |

## Locked-stack overrides for this app

If you use a dep that is not in ADR-001, list it here with rationale; the auditor consults this section before flagging.

```
# Example
- react-native-svg@^15.0.0: SVG rendering (RN locked stack has no SVG primitive yet).
  Added 2026-06-25 by @atul. Tracked for ADR-001 upstream addition: <ticket>.
```

## Parity manifest

Used by `bin/bstack-mobile-parity` to detect iOS↔Android drift. List every user-facing feature that should be at parity; the parity tool can compare perm + capability declarations.

```
# Example
- camera_scan: iOS+Android, requires camera perm
- biometric_unlock: iOS+Android, no perm (uses LocalAuthentication / BiometricPrompt)
- push_notifications: iOS+Android, requires POST_NOTIFICATIONS (Android 13+) / UNUserNotificationCenter
```

If a feature is intentionally one-platform-only, declare it here so the parity tool doesn't flag it:

```
- live_activities: iOS-only (Android has no equivalent — accepted)
- widgets_homescreen: iOS+Android (different implementations)
```

## On-call

| Role | Owner |
|---|---|
| Primary on-call | <github-handle> (rotated weekly, see #on-call) |
| Mobile reviewer | `@bstack-mobile-reviewers` GitHub team |
| Native escape-hatch owner (if `apps/native-*`) | <github-handle> |

## Release runbooks

- Store release: `/bstack:mobile-release` then follow the prompt.
- OTA hotfix: `/bstack:hotfix` then follow the OTA branch.
- Signing-key compromise: `docs/runbooks/MOBILE-SIGNING-COMPROMISE.md`.

## Reviewer escape hatches (per-app overrides)

Some rules support per-app override with explicit rationale. Document overrides here:

```
# Example
- parity-ignore: live_activities — iOS-only by product decision (no Android equivalent shipped).
- targetSdk-grace: 2026-08 window for API 36 bump tracked in <ticket>.
```
